    "proved": "Ordinary and ideal projections of a sum of arbitrary curve potentials under a separated smooth obstacle are exactly the sums of the corresponding curve projections. The curve backgrounds are arbitrary smooth admissible forms, including zero area. The identity requires separated obstacles and does not factor arbitrary obstacles on the product.",
    "mechanism": "Coordinatewise competitors give the lower ordinary bound. A regularized partial supremum and genuine slice induction give its upper bound, with poles handled by the original singularity bound. Atomic Green potentials and smooth gauges produce finite-mass countable coordinate divisor currents; divisor domination and ideal obstacle reprojection give the ideal identity. Zero-area factors have smooth potentials and are treated directly.",
    "retained_boundary": "Only sums of curve potentials under separated smooth obstacles are projected coordinatewise. This result makes no zero-volume claim on Y, no arbitrary-obstacle factorization and no unrestricted higher-dimensional completion claim."
  },
